-- title:
--   Toric points lie in the kernel of both degeneracy push-forwards
-- statement:
--   Fix natural numbers $N_0$ and $p$ with $N_0 \neq 0$, with $p$ prime and non-zero, and assume $p \nmid N_0$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbf{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` with `A.LiesOverPrime p`, i.e. the image of $p$ in $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$ lies in the non-units of $A$. Let $\Lambda$ be a `LevelData N₀ p A`: a morphism $\sigma_A$ from $\operatorname{Spec} A$ to the base scheme `base p` satisfying `barPt A ≫ σA = genPt p`, a scheme $X$ with a morphism $f$ to `base p`, a relative group law $L$ on $f$ over `baseRing p`, and bijections `pts` from $J_0(N_0)$-classes `JZero N₀` onto the sections of $f$ over the generic point and `ptsSp` from `JZeroC (ResidueField A) N₀` onto the sections over `resPt A ≫ σA`. Assume $\Lambda$ satisfies `IsJacobian`, the conjunction of: the abelian-scheme property bundle for $f$, commutativity of $L$, additivity of `pts` and of `ptsSp`, Galois equivariance of `pts`, agreement of reduction of points modulo $\ell$ whenever the corresponding inputs hold, and the existence, for each element of the Hecke algebra, of an endomorphism of $f$ compatible with $L$ and inducing the Hecke action on `pts`. Let $O$ be a `JZeroNeronObjectAtP N₀ p hpN₀ A hA Λ` (a smooth separated group scheme $g$ over `base p` with commutative relative group law, Galois- and Hecke-equivariant parametrisation of `JZero (N₀ * p)`, flat surjective multiplication-by-$n$, proper generic fibre, a toric rank and the attendant data), and let $m > 0$. The conclusion is that every $x$ in `O.toricPts m` — for $m > 0$ the subgroup of `JZero (N₀ * p)` generated by the range of `O.toricPoint m hm` — is annihilated by both components of `degeneracyPushforwardPair N₀ p`, i.e. $\alpha_* x = 0$ and $\beta_* x = 0$, where these are the two push-forward homomorphisms `JZero (N₀ * p) →+ JZero N₀` along `heckeAlphaBar` and `heckeBetaBar` when the predicate `DegeneracyPushforwardInputs N₀ p` holds, and the zero maps otherwise.
--
--   This is the statement that the toric part of the Néron object at $p$ of level $N_0p$ consists of $p$-new classes: the group generated by the $\overline{\mathbf{Q}}$-points of the toric lift lies in the intersection of the kernels of the two degeneracy push-forwards $J_0(N_0p) \to J_0(N_0)$. It is used in the construction of the ordinary/toric data at $p$ and in results extracting $m$-divisibility and Hecke relations on toric points.
